r  eight months completely alone didn't  really bother me overall because i had  windows so in here much much much harder  but that's that's my main downside  there's a little bit of dirt just kind  of started to annoy me  i think in large part because it leaned  into my concerns with having asked me  that  all the time so it's it's for the  greater good but it is still something  that you know regardless of being aware  of all of those things was  very tough to deal with mentally is  is just stupid thing about having asthma  is knowing that your own body is trying  to suffocate you from the inside out too  it's just like can you just [ __ ]  leave me alone because it's just your  own [ __ ] chest doing it to you  there were also some moments where  um my internet connection dropped  infrequently not something that was  hugely prohibitive for me just a thing  to note for anyone going through this  largely the internet in this hotel was  wonderful i had 200 up to 200 down i was  able to stream  i was able to upload youtube videos it  was it was great um i was able to work  have video calls all that good stuff  just a couple of hiccups nothing major  yeah the only other thing is there are a  couple of times where they forgot to  bring me food they  didn't bring me lunch on two separate  days  very weird but i wasn't really worried  about it because i  i frankly ate way too much while i was  in here anyway because i think i liked  the routine of like the food arrives at  this time and you have an activity at  this time but those are the only  real major negatives that that i felt um  i will also say i have a beautiful view  here like an absolutely beautiful view  so like i can show you now this is  darling harbour in sydney and it is  lovely  um watching the sunrise come over that  every day it was beautiful it was it was  so nice  so no real downside there i'm probably  gonna miss seeing the sunrise if  anything it's been it's been  lovely i did also end up in the uh  end of this whole thing just  got way more alcohol than i would have  expected like  i got beer delivered from a friend and  then the hotel just kept delivering me  like wine and stuff some of those i did  opt into but they gave me more than i  asked for  by a lot and i got a bunch of cider that  was definitely a thing ended up  delivering a lot more alcohol than i  thought and i yeah i did successfully  get some food delivered through ubereats  but overall you know a totally fine  experience uh  nothing extremely outlying like i feel  like there were more positives than i  expected which is that it went past  really fast and um i wasn't bored at all  and i was able to work out i just  cleared some stuff here and had a  perfect vr  setup space internet was strong and  solid and the food was actually really  good  obviously the downside being the asthma  not really being able to  clean in any way that i would have liked  to um  i think i said you can take your sheets  and put them outside and order new  sheets and all that stuff so you can do  laundry for your sheets and your towels  but  that's the extent of that really i i've  worn the same clothes intentionally over  and over again though this i realized i  got  some food on so we're gonna need to wash  that as soon as we get out of here but  yeah that's pretty much it just kind of  wanted to go over  sort of what this was like fill in any  information that i feel like would be  helpful to people who might go through  it but i don't think i have anything  else to add so yeah please do let me  know if you have any questions i will  help out as much as i can  um with anyone who might have questions  and  yeah i'm really excited to get to see my  family  it is a very exciting time i don't know  what my internet connection is going to  be like as soon as i leave here  so i don't know what's going to happen  to streams or uploads  now between my mom and my dad's houses  which i assume will have different  speeds i don